ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"1d9df52151ec899994343d7ac3487cb1634109ace20bed4a57bab593736be839","event_uuid":"c4dbb45c-86d5-4df9-b63f-56bfbcf03abc","position":{"commit_sha":"1089affa922feed06588250f897ca7da37a77552","position":"1787027971960982001-c4dbb45c-86d5-4df9-b63f-56bfbcf03abc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d9e248d3840dbb65cacea3c2b40ccb1ad4aa457d97e7f62163a6c37fbf24b977","event_uuid":"d2abcca6-e3a2-429f-8534-59b2e4b9bfeb","position":{"commit_sha":"71c43cca0872a4f5bcdf4d9a7f1bffd23ad6003e","position":"1787027990716156001-d2abcca6-e3a2-429f-8534-59b2e4b9bfeb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787027941603250001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"c4dbb45c-86d5-4df9-b63f-56bfbcf03abc","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"a8cd-01cd-c370-454f"},{"link_uuid":"d2abcca6-e3a2-429f-8534-59b2e4b9bfeb","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"c6f3-cda5-c460-4c5c"}],"description":"## Context\nCloud/DC atomic executors need a core route that bypasses generic retry without falsely advancing the current handler baseline. Production must remain on legacy until S3 validates and cuts over.\n\n## Outcome\nAdd a constructor-injected legacy-default selector for exact summary updates, map confirmed outcomes through the existing result surface, and expose terminal outcomes as bounded per-mutation errors without baseline/provenance advance. Finalize the S1 section of ADR 0100.\n\n## Plan\n1. Route only exact `{\"summary\"}` when tests explicitly enable the selector. Mixed fields remain one unsplit legacy call. Add no config/env key and never dual-send.\n2. Poison-test generic `_call_with_retry` on the selected route. Preserve every unselected route.\n3. Map success/recovered success to legacy result, `_fields_synced`, `_comment_errors`, and `_subop` shapes.\n4. Map `commit_unknown`/`retry_not_before` to an internal tagged result consumed by `handle_update`; record a bounded per-mutation error/disposition, keep `_fields_synced` empty, advance no baseline/provenance, persist no S1 deferral, and continue the batch.\n5. Name S3 as sole cutover, fuse/deferral consumer, and bridge-retirement owner in contract/ADR.\n\n## Testing\nUse exact-versus-mixed routing tables, poison retries, Cloud/DC verified fakes, and apply-handler baseline/provenance spies.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The internal selector defaults to legacy and adds no config or environment key.\n- [ ] Test-enabled exact summary bypasses generic retry, while mixed fields remain one legacy call.\n- [ ] Confirmed Cloud/DC outcomes preserve all existing result and telemetry shapes.\n- [ ] Terminal outcomes record bounded per-mutation errors and never advance baseline or provenance.\n- [ ] Terminal outcomes persist no deferral in S1 and do not stop unrelated batch work.\n- [ ] ADR 0100 names S3 as sole production cutover, fuse/deferral consumer, and compatibility-bridge retirement owner.\n\n## Out of scope\nDefault-on routing, fuse behavior, and durable deferral remain RP-03 S3.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_one.py","reason":"Add the legacy-default exact-summary selector and outcome mapping."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_apply_phases.py","reason":"Bypass and poison-test generic retry on the selected route."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_handlers.py","reason":"Consume terminal tags without false baseline/provenance advance."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_operation_retry_budget.py","reason":"Cross-provider routing and compatibility tests."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_apply_handlers_operation_outcome.py","reason":"Handler result, error, baseline, and provenance regressions."},{"path":"docs/adr/0100-reconciler-operation-coordination.md","reason":"Finalize S1 lifecycle ownership and cutover boundaries."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","a8cd-01cd-c370-454f"],["depends_on","c6f3-cda5-c460-4c5c"],["parent","f5ac-6373-5e33-4374"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"f5ac-6373-5e33-4374","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["rp03","retry","reconciler","tdd","adr"],"ticket_id":"72d0-0f09-1694-4010","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-03 S1 T4 — Integrate the summary executor behind the legacy-default seam","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_operation_retry_budget.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_apply_handlers_operation_outcome.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_applier_retry.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC5","dd_text":"Selector, routing, result compatibility, terminal error, and no false state advance"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_check_docs_index.py tests/scripts/test_check_adr_numbers.py","dd_id":"AC6","dd_text":"ADR lifecycle ownership and documentation index"}]},"source_event_uuids":["71bf5db7-8e91-4675-bb5b-f0c50a3ac635","d709b172-ce77-4eca-98ed-07f92278ff8c","60e8f5d